-- ============================================ THE HOLES COLUMN (w_agg_overflow_holes)
-- What a hole leaves out is not known to be false, in both engines: two
-- worlds with no aggregate, answered by both (docs/aggregates.md, "Holes, as
-- built"; f_a_negation_of_what_a_hole_left_out_succeeds).
-- Int is ±2^60 in both engines: every operator past the range at both ends,
-- -2^60 a value, exact results past 2^53, the signs of / and mod, and a
-- literal of 2^60 refused (f_arithmetic_wraps_past_the_term_range). Two
-- engines answer it, so a fault in either one's `is` reds it.
